  "full_response": "Here's a guide to integrating your Slack app with a webhook. This guide includes creating a webhook URL and using the necessary token to secure your connections. It will also showcase how to format your payloads to mention users and channels.\n\n### Step 1: Generating a Slack Webhook URL\n\n1. Navigate to the **[Slack API](https://api.slack.com/)** portal and find the **\" Webhooks\"** feature.\n\n2. Click on **'Add to Slack'** and choose anywhere within your Slack workspace.\n\n3. Slack will provide you with a unique Webhook URL.\n\n4. You can safely copy this URL. It will look something like this:\n\n    ```\n    https://hooks.slack.com/services/T00000000/B00000000/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\n    ```\n\n   The part that starts with **T00000000** is the token, which ensures secure communication.\n\n### Step 2: Embedding the Token and Webhook in Payloads\n\nWe’ll use this example payload to show how to mention users and channels:\n\n```json\n{\n    \"text\": \"This is a sample notification from the webhook\",\n    \"username\": \"Webhook App\",\n    \"channel_id\": \"C1234567890\",\n    \"attachments\": [\n        {\n            \"text\": \"Please take a look at this \\n- **Link to our report** \\n- https://example.com/reports/2023-Winter\",\n            \"mrkdwn_in\": [\"text\", \"fields\"],\n            \"fields\": [\n                {\n                    \"title\": \"Requested By\",\n                    \"value\": \"John Doe <john@company.com>\",\n                    \"short\": true\n                },\n                {\n                    \"title\": \"Created By\",\n                    \"value\": \"Slack Bot\",\n                    \"short\": true\n                }\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"text\": \"Let's get a meeting scheduled with @JaneDoe and @JohnSmith to discuss updates.\",\n            \"mrkdwn_in\": [\"text\"]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n### Step 3: Posting a Notification with Mentioned Users and Channels\n\nTo post a notification with the structure mentioned above, simply send a POST request using the Webhook URL from your server or frontend application, filling in the appropriate values.\n\nHere's how you might do it in a Node.js application:\n\n```javascript\nconst axios = require('axios');\n\n// Replace 'WEBHOC_SLACK_URL' with your actual Webhook URL\nconst webhookUrl = 'WEBHOC_SLACK_URL';\n\n//",
